://api.github.com/users/coinerd","html_url":"https://github.com/coinerd","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coinerd/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coinerd/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coinerd/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coinerd/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coinerd/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coinerd/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coinerd/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coinerd/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coinerd/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"jobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coinerd/q/actions/runs/36341632075/jobs","logs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coinerd/q/actions/runs/36341632075/logs","check_suite_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coinerd/q/check-suites/98403555958","artifacts_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coinerd/q/actions/runs/36341632075/artifacts","cancel_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coinerd/q/actions/runs/36341632075/cancel","rerun_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coinerd/q/actions/runs/36341632075/rerun","previous_attempt_url":null,"workflow_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coinerd/q/actions/workflows/259542599","head_commit":{"id":"c5375e605bc9a724b4b105ce5697e0e774a271bd","tree_id":"70b1ddc46edd926d95b8ddf9f34a73df5939f4dd","message":"fix(release): give the release test lane full history so the recorded rehearsal head resolves\n\nThe v1.00.31 release run failed in its `test` job before reaching `prepare`:\n`tests/test-wave-integrity-adversarial.rkt` reported 7 passed / 1 failed, and the\nfailing assertion was \"the rehearsal head is present in this repository\"\n(tests/test-wave-integrity-adversarial.rkt:216).\n\nThat test asserts the recorded `rehearsal-head` (50bdf7334) is a commit the\nrepository actually contains. The release `test` job checked out with the\ndefault `fetch-depth: 1`, so a head predating the checkout tip is unresolvable\nand the assertion is false in CI while true in a full clone. This was never a\nproperty of the W6 rehearsal artifact: the recorded head is a real main\nancestor and is present in a complete clone.\n\nThis is the same defect, and the same repair, already applied in `ci.yml` for\nthis exact test, whose `fetch-depth: 0` comment names it. The release lane was\nthe sibling that was missed, which is why main CI passed and the release failed.\nThe `preflight` job in the same workflow already used `fetch-depth: 0` for\nprecisely this class of history-dependent check.\n\nDiagnosis, not a guess. Reproduced by cloning the published `v1.00.31` tag at\ndepth 1 and running the test unmodified: 7 passed, 1 failed, same assertion.\n`git fetch --unshallow` on that same clone makes `git cat-file -t\n50bdf7334...` resolve to `commit` and the same unmodified test then passes\n8/8. The fix is the checkout depth alone.\n\nThe test was deliberately NOT weakened. Making it tolerate a shallow clone\nwould have meant editing `tests/test-wave-integrity-adversarial.rkt`, which is\nitself one of the nine digest-bound `rehearsal-inputs` in the W6 injection\nmatrix, so that edit would invalidate the recorded matrix and\n`rehearsal-inputs-digest` and force a W6 artifact regeneration. Fixing the\ncheckout rather than the assertion keeps the provenance binding intact and\npreserves the assertion's teeth: a genuinely fabricated head still fails.\n\nVerification: workflows contract 7/7, purge contract 15/15, W9 workflow\nverification 18/18, compiled-root workflow 113/113, CI runtime contract 38/38;\nlint-all 23 passed with 2 warnings (unchanged); release notes and the\nversion-expectation lint over 1511 test files clean. YAML re-parsed to confirm\n`fetch-depth: 0` lands on the `test` job and that no other step changed.\n\nThe annotated tag `v1.00.31` remains pointed at the release that failed; it will\nbe retagged at the head carrying this fix so the published release is one whose\nrelease lane actually passed end to end.","timestamp":"2026-09-27T18:20:27Z","author":{"name":"CI Fixture","email":"ci@example.invalid"},"committer":{"name":"CI Fixture","email":"ci@example.invalid"}},"repository":{"id":1204314088,"node_id":"R_kgDOR8hf6A","name":"q","full_name":"coinerd/q","private":false,"owner":{"login":"coinerd","id":10107520,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTA3NTIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10107520?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coinerd","html_url":"https://github.com/coinerd","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coinerd/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coinerd/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coinerd/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coinerd/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coinerd/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coinerd/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coinerd/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coinerd/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coinerd/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"html_url":"https://github.com/coinerd/q","description":"racket coding agent","fork":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coinerd/q","forks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coinerd/q/forks","keys_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coinerd/q/keys{/key_id}","collaborators_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coinerd/q/collaborators{/collaborator}","teams_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coinerd/q/teams","hooks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coinerd/q/hooks","issue_events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coinerd/q/issues/events{/number}","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coinerd/q/events","assignees_url":"https://api.github.com/r